content.text:
Diagnosed and fixed. The durable run failed only in the final action-pin verifier because it assumed `rg` was available on the release runner. All substantive checks before it passed; no release-plan, build, approval, or publishing job ran.

I opened [PR #41](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/41) with the portable fix:

- uses Git to enumerate tracked workflow/action YAML;
- uses standard `grep`, available on the runner image;
- verified with a minimal `PATH=/usr/bin:/bin`, ShellCheck, Actionlint, and diff checks.

Once #41 merges, the next `main` push will exercise the corrected no-release path.

I completed the broader audit and found one additional real release-only gap before it could surprise us:

- PR #40 upgrades attestation to v4. Its underlying `actions/attest` requires `artifact-metadata: write`; the durable build job lacked it. Ordinary PR CI cannot reach that approval-gated build path, so it would otherwise fail only during a real release.

I added the least-privilege permission and a prevention mechanism to [PR #41](https://github.com/orin-dx/callisto/pull/41):

- portable action-pin verifier—no `rg` assumption;
- new early **Workflow Contracts** job;
- both release shell contracts run with `PATH=/usr/bin:/bin`;
- validation waits for that contract job;
- v4 attestation permission is present.

Validation completed locally: minimal-path tests, ShellCheck, Actionlint, and `just ci-fast` with all 1,256 tests passing.

PR #40’s seven CI checks are green. Merge #41 before PR #40, so the permission is in place when the v4 attestation upgrade lands.

